# Protection's prevention and Ancient Adamantoise's redirection both want to change the 2 damage Pyroclasm would deal to
# Bot1's Llanowar Elves, which Mother of Runes has given protection from red: the Elves' controller chooses which applies
# first (CR 616.1). Bot1 has it redirected, so it would be dealt to the Adamantoise, whose own protection is judged now
# (CR 614.6) - it has none, and the Elves' no longer applies to it (CR 616.1f). The Adamantoise takes 2 for the Elves, 2 for
# Mother of Runes and its own 2: 6, and every creature lives. The other order is
# ancient-adamantoise-pyroclasm-on-a-protected-elf-its-controller-prevents-it-first.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Show and Tell
Ancient Adamantoise
Forest
Mox Pearl
Mother of Runes
Llanowar Elves
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Pyroclasm
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Ancient Adamantoise)
Bot2.Choose()
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mother of Runes.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Pyroclasm.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mother of Runes.Activate(Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Colors(Red)
Bot1.Replace(Ancient Adamantoise)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Ancient Adamantoise.Damage = 6
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Damage = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Mother of Runes.Damage = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Pyroclasm
